      "a": "We need to find the input value for which the function will not be derivable. In other words, the point where the function has a break (there are two different tangents at that point)\n$f\\left( x \\right) = \\left\\{ \\begin{align} 2x - 7\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x \\geqslant \\dfrac{7}{2} \\hfill \\\\ 7 - 2x\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x < \\dfrac{7}{2} \\hfill \\\\ \\end{align}\u00a0 \\right.$\nHence, for the value $x = \\dfrac{7}{2}$, the function is not derivable."
